<div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1235866#post1235866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The playtest document didn't have anything about Limit in there. It was really about 5% character creation and 95% Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are lunar occult charms?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T05:12:11-07:00","id":1235871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1235870#post1235870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are lunar occult charms?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, honestly we didn't get much of a chance to see those. Maybe it's due to the fact there aren't strictly occult charms? The whole book is organized by Attribute, not Ability. But, I can look through now and see how they fare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T12:22:52-07:00","id":1236062,"title":"","content":"Does it feel radically different to 2nd ed Lunars, or more like familiar Lunars but good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T12:24:32-07:00","id":1236063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1235870#post1235870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are lunar occult charms?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are some really cool Mysticism charms under the Perception Branch. There is one that let's you attempt to grapple a dematerialized entity and upon succeeding causing it to materialize for the duration of the grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T12:29:31-07:00","id":1236066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236062#post1236062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it feel radically different to 2nd ed Lunars, or more like familiar Lunars but good?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's got a lot of the 2nd edition feel but some charms are a little different because of the new combat system of 3rd edition. The Totemic stuff is really cool, instead of traveling down a particular charm branch and picking up 4 or 5 charms that your character will never use, you can hop into a charm tree if it is Totemic. For example, you may be looking at a DEX charm that is 3 or 4 charms down a tree and one will pop up that allows you to take it if you meet other requirements. It would say something like &quot;if your spirit shape is Legendary then you can take this strength charm as a Stamina charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T12:34:07-07:00","id":1236068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReformedNinja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236063#post1236063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some really cool Mysticism charms under the Perception Branch. There is one that let's you attempt to grapple a dematerialized entity and upon succeeding causing it to materialize for the duration of the grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kinda reminds me of a fight my seafaring group's Abyssal had with one of Siakal's kin. Only she put the thing in a headlock while it was still material, and just kept holding on while it dematerialized, until she'd finally choked it out. Did some real damage to her hands, but the shark-god definitely got the worse end of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T12:39:46-07:00","id":1236070,"title":"","content":"Oh man, this sounds like all the cool stuff we've ever wanted! Any weird charms in Intelligence that jumped out to you? I keep wondering how they do the whole Establishing Facts thing with a Lunary flair. Or general oddness that results when you have Raw Intelligence as a power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:00:32-07:00","id":1236083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReformedNinja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236066#post1236066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's got a lot of the 2nd edition feel but some charms are a little different because of the new combat system of 3rd edition. The Totemic stuff is really cool, instead of traveling down a particular charm branch and picking up 4 or 5 charms that your character will never use, you can hop into a charm tree if it is Totemic. For example, you may be looking at a DEX charm that is 3 or 4 charms down a tree and one will pop up that allows you to take it if you meet other requirements. It would say something like &amp;quot;if your spirit shape is Legendary then you can take this strength charm as a Stamina charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of non-mechanical totemic requirements are there? You mentioned creatures that live in a hive. <br /> Are most of them mechanical (eg legendary size) or non-mechanical?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:05:06-07:00","id":1236089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236083#post1236083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of non-mechanical totemic requirements are there? You mentioned creatures that live in a hive.<br /> Are most of them mechanical (eg legendary size) or non-mechanical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like most of the charms with the totemic keyword are based on your spirit shape. Like &quot;if your spirit shape hunts in packs&quot; then you can get this or &quot;if your spirit shape is a prey animal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:20:29-07:00","id":1236104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236070#post1236070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man, this sounds like all the cool stuff we've ever wanted! Any weird charms in Intelligence that jumped out to you? I keep wondering how they do the whole Establishing Facts thing with a Lunary flair. Or general oddness that results when you have Raw Intelligence as a power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did see a cool Intelligence Crafting charm that allowed you to make articles of clothing that are of the none armor type where you can put dots of mutations into the item. The wearer of the item takes on the mutations that you instilled into the item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:23:36-07:00","id":1236108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReformedNinja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236104#post1236104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did see a cool Intelligence Crafting charm that allowed you to make articles of clothing that are of the none armor type where you can put dots of mutations into the item. The wearer of the item takes on the mutations that you instilled into the item.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that like mutating an existing article of clothing, or...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/J1HBhdp_XR0?t=26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/J1HBhdp_XR0?t=26\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/J1HBhdp_XR0?t=26\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/J1HBhdp_XR0?t=26 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T14:35:52-07:00","id":1236149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236070#post1236070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man, this sounds like all the cool stuff we've ever wanted! Any weird charms in Intelligence that jumped out to you? I keep wondering how they do the whole Establishing Facts thing with a Lunary flair. Or general oddness that results when you have Raw Intelligence as a power.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is my job to answer this in the next episode. I\u2019ll be covering the \u2018No Moon\u2019 or mental archetypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T14:37:08-07:00","id":1236151,"title":"","content":"Hell yeah! Been telling folks to check it next week for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:07:36-07:00","id":1236167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236149#post1236149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is my job to answer this in the next episode. I\u2019ll be covering the \u2018No Moon\u2019 or mental archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I used to play a No Moon, and have a lot of No Moon concepts, but they were pretty under-supported in the new edition.<br /> <br /> What anima powers have you guys found really fun and exciting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T20:08:28-07:00","id":1236273,"title":"","content":"So I went through your archives a bit and I liked what I read so far. There's soem cool stuff in there, and I think you guys do a surprisngly good job of being able to make an interesting podcast about, while my favorite fictional setting, one I was not sure you could do a podcast about. Good stuff.<br /> <br /> I do have a bit of a critique in that I went through your three-part &quot;Exatled as a whole&quot; thing, and I will say that while I appreciate your description of Creation's history, I think that for a podcast that tries to hype the game as it is, it does I think lean a bit on things that were true of 2e but not true of 3e, and were also not true of 2e either at least how you said them. Not sure if you want such corrections, but it is something that stood out ot me a bit and something that kind of I admit feel like I would have to correct to players if they were new to the setting and were to listen through it.<br /> <br /> But in any case, good stuff, and I've subscribed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:06:01-07:00","id":1236344,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> Yes, I know that there are some inter-edition inconsistencies with the setting piece. Some of it I feel is appropriate (like not getting bogged down with whether there are exactly 300 solar exaltations), and some of it might possibly merit an edit (like whether or not Gaia\u2019s body forms the surface of the world). Also, when I say something like the Neverborn created the Contagion, but I don\u2019t mention the Deathlords, it\u2019s really for the sake of simplicity. I know that those kinds of things mildly irritate people who know the setting really well, and all of its changes across editions, but I wasn\u2019t really aiming it at those people. I was trying to be brief and tell it like I would (and did) to my own children to get them to understand. That all being said, if there are some particular facts that you think would be important to change, by all means please let me know. Like I said, I am already considering changing the Gaia statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:18:10-07:00","id":1236438,"title":"","content":"For me the big ones were these, if it helps if you ever edit. Overall it's great, but I think it's worth highlighting I guess:<br /> - Primordial as a term in itself isn't actually used in 3e. It might someday, but right now isn't.<br /> <br /> - Gaia, as you note, didn't use her body for Creation. The Dragons aren't her souls or at least, not necessarily her souls in 3e either. They're her Chidlren and obviously important to Creation's well, creation, but we don't know much beyond that this time around.<br /> <br /> - The five Reclamation Yozi in 2e weren't the only Yozi then, but the way you phrased it in the episode kind of implied they did. This is just a slight editting bug. In 3e though, it's worth remembering that Infernals are not tied to speciifc Yozis but draw on Hellish themes and the Yozis more broadly.<br /> <br /> - There are actually about 300-400 Lunars this time around.<br /> <br /> - Autochthon's involvement in the creation of the Exalted is not so clear this time around. Note that the 3e coreobok more or less says the Sun started the get-together and doesn't mention him at all. I'd mostly jut de-emphasize the hows of Exaltation and such and focus on the whole &quot;Gods got together and used humans as mistletoe&quot; thing. I think here things would have been better to go like with the Deathlords. The specifics are less important than the broaders troke actions and events.<br /> <br /> - I'm guessing when we know more about Liminals and Exigents you'll put htem in but yeah, here it seems a bit a good idea to omit. Not relaly an issue, just something I observed.<br /> <br /> Hope this is helpful at all. I don't want to come accross as overly pedantic, but I like what you're doing and want it to be as good as it can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:42:58-07:00","id":1236446,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the list! It\u2019s helpful.<br /> <br /> In a lot of these areas, though, I feel like there should be a generous orthodoxy. When we\u2019re talking about a new edition that hasn\u2019t really given us many details yet on some of this stuff, I feel like it\u2019s not useful to split hairs. Like the whole \u2018primordial\u2019 thing. I mean, you can\u2019t just go around all day saying \u201cThe Enemy of the Gods\u201d. It\u2019s clunky, and sometimes you just need a simple word.<br /> <br /> Also there isn\u2019t really an Infernals canon yet. We have the preview document from the Kickstarter, but that is very sketchy and subject to change. So in those areas, I have to stick to what sounds good. Same with Autochthon. When new books come out addressing some of these things, I can change those portions, but I\u2019m not going to do it based on dev forum posts or whatnot.<br /> <br /> Gaia is another story, as I noted above. Do you happen to have a page reference right off hand for her role in the new edition, and you\u2019re the second person to say that the Dragons aren\u2019t her component souls, but do you have a reference for that as well? I\u2019ve been meaning to do a big research project on that, but I haven\u2019t had time yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:16:20-07:00","id":1236457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236446#post1236446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you\u2019re the second person to say that the Dragons aren\u2019t her component souls, but do you have a reference for that as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no explicit single sentence in Ex3 that says they're specifically not component souls, no, but <i>every </i>instance of the Dragons being referenced in relation to Gaia in Ex3 refers to them only as her children.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:47:47-07:00","id":1236476,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s also worth noting that this time around, the elemental poles and elementals predate Yu-Shan and the gods.<br /> <br /> Previously, the gods created the five original elementals, which the Primordials destroyed and from the pieces of which the lesser elementals were born.<br /> <br /> Now, those original elementals might not exist at all. Or they were slain by the Primordials and used to make the poles. Or they still live.<br /> <br /> Gaia might have procreated with those five original elementals (or maybe had landscape sex with the poles themselves) to bear the Five Dragons as behemoth children.<br /> <br /> Similar to how Adjoran birthed four behemoth living-wind creatures by having dream sex with a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:55:46-07:00","id":1236478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236446#post1236446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the list! It\u2019s helpful.<br /> <br /> In a lot of these areas, though, I feel like there should be a generous orthodoxy. When we\u2019re talking about a new edition that hasn\u2019t really given us many details yet on some of this stuff, I feel like it\u2019s not useful to split hairs. Like the whole \u2018primordial\u2019 thing. I mean, you can\u2019t just go around all day saying \u201cThe Enemy of the Gods\u201d. It\u2019s clunky, and sometimes you just need a simple word.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are actually some terms you used I'd just use more of in there. Creators, titans, makers, all that. I think for 3e to me the big thing is thesaurus it up. I remember why it was avoided form the previous devs was apparently that they were just over-used and everything relevant in Creation felt ultimatley tied to a Primordial somehow. By avoiding the term and talking with them in prose, it kind of created distance. The term might have shown up again by thier watch, but they wanted to give &quot;breathing room&quot; to it if that makes any sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236446#post1236446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there isn\u2019t really an Infernals canon yet. We have the preview document from the Kickstarter, but that is very sketchy and subject to change. So in those areas, I have to stick to what sounds good. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Here the big thing is just expand the Five in previous editions. Those five were focused on in the 2e Infernals book as I understand it not becuase they had any real significance over other Yozis, but becuase they were the ones with bigger write-ups in the original <b>Games of Divinity</b> book. I even at times wonder if they were given the Castes they were because that's the order they were described in tha toriginal book and nothing more.<br /> <br /> This one was more just pointing out though your thing says that the five were <i>the</i> five survivors of the War of the Gods. Which isn't quite right, and what I more was pushing against. And I think just not stating Caste associations with them (Have to relisten if you did say that) is something I'd avoid. They're champions of the Yozis as a whole, not just the five, basically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236446#post1236446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Same with Autochthon. When new books come out addressing some of these things, I can change those portions, but I\u2019m not going to do it based on dev forum posts or whatnot.\\\\</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for this, it would have been a better treatment ot just avoid him altogether, much like you did with the Deathlords and the Contagion. He ultimately is ancillary to the goals of the gods, their creating Chosen and his presence after the beginning of history. Rather than him coming to show them secrets and build them Exaltations, which in 3e I think he specifically <i>didn't</i> do or not in the wya described, best leave him out and say it how it was in the corebook. The gods found a way and used that way. He's a neat bit of the setting but ultimatley, quite superfluous to understanding it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236446#post1236446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia is another story, as I noted above. Do you happen to have a page reference right off hand for her role in the new edition, and you\u2019re the second person to say that the Dragons aren\u2019t her component souls, but do you have a reference for that as well? I\u2019ve been meaning to do a big research project on that, but I haven\u2019t had time yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragons at least implis they are not the same thing as a demon soul by their description:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Third Edition, p. 61</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Five Elemental Dragons</b><br /> Not gods or demons, nor mere elementals rising fromCreation\u2019s Essence, the Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia\u2019s children. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Lexicon entry also calls them &quot;children of Gaia&quot;, but not her souls. Gaia's Lexicon entry also says this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Exalted Third Edition, p. 27</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Gaia: </b>A spirit of vast creative force, she is the mother of<br /> the <i>Five Elementla Dragons </i>...</div> </div> </div> </div>The most in-depth thing on the matter I could find was by SLS early on in the 3e timieline of things, but i'm sure Robert of Eric said so also, just have to spend more time digging the Ask the Devs thread:<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/6495\" target=\"_blank\">http://nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/6495</a><br /> <br /> The short take here is they aren't specifically her souls this edition. They're her children,w hatever that might be. it coudl be souls. It could also just be weird things based from her, like Adrojan's own daughters which aren't demons either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:15:04-07:00","id":1236487,"title":"","content":"Would they be \u201cdemons\u201d if Gaia isn\u2019t imprisoned in Malfeas with the Yozis? Whatever they are, do they kind of fill the same role as component souls? The reason I ask is because they are such a big part of Creation that it is essentially defined by their summation - very much like component souls.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not trying to defend my language. I\u2019m really just trying to figure out what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:18:03-07:00","id":1236488,"title":"","content":"I find it worth noting that all three editions of Exalted have referred to the 5EDs as children of Gaia in their lexicon entries. They were likely never intended to be an equivalent to her 3rd circle souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:39:25-07:00","id":1236495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236487#post1236487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do they kind of fill the same role as component souls? The reason I ask is because they are such a big part of Creation that it is essentially defined by their summation - very much like component souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation is not Gaia, though; also Creation is not &quot;essentially defined by&quot; the Elemental Dragons - the poles at which they reside embody the elements of Creation, but that's hardly the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1236487#post1236487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m really just trying to figure out what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's what we're trying to tell you - an introductory course in the Exalted RPG does not require you to explain everything, especially not the stuff that's been intentionally left a mystery.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:09:34-07:00","id":1236525,"title":"","content":"More or less. The big thing is we don't know what the Dragons are exactly. They could be her souls, but in 3e, that question is left intentionally open. All that can be sais is they're her children and divinities on par with the Incarna. Beyond that, they don't need to have much said about them I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:14:42-07:00","id":1236529,"title":"","content":"For my take, they're probably like, template beings like a behemoth, but on a much grander scale to be divinities. I kind of like this idea that they're maybe even the things that built the poles or whatnot, or that they exist as the Platonic idea of &quot;being made of this kind of element&quot; that then had some role int he creation of other behemoths or naimals in Creation in general. But in the end, beings of Creation not Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T19:37:02-07:00","id":1236982,"title":"","content":"So randomly listening through another episode, your one on the Caul was neat. Bit late on things, but some comments that came up:<br /> <br /> <b>On Iconic Characters</b><br /> The term I use for characters like Chejob Kejak, Sha'a Oka, or Mnemon is less &quot;metaplot&quot; character and more just &quot;canon character&quot;. I think the way to think of it is metaplot in the context of World of Darkness meant that there was an ongoing plot, book to book, whcih changed the setting over time. Things like that were how in Vampire: the Masquerade, the Assamites broke the Tremere cruse, Salubri <i>antitribu</i> and Harbingers of Skulls joined the Sabbat, Ravnos had the Week of Nightmares, and so on. And notably, events would happen in one book and the books from then on would incoreprate that into canon. Some of these happened in sourcebooks, but others did happen in novels or pieces of ficiton.<br /> <br /> Exalted has not really ever had this, save I would say the Scarelt Empress bredcrumb trail that ramped up through 2e. But most of the game is set in RY 768 and things are written form this &quot;Day Zero&quot; framework much of the time. Events in novels were not canon in 1e at least, and tehre was actually a lot of consternation when there were attempts to do so. But I think metaplot doesn't fit htese characters. They're assumed to exist in the world canonically though, which is why I use canon isntead of metaplot. <br /> <br /> Another term used is signature characters, which is something often I find ascribed to canonical characters in Exalted and other WW games. This is often used specifically for characters who are representitive of splats in teh way you note iconics. In 1e they were the ones you saw in splats, as well as the different Exalts having a &quot;general&quot; sig' to them a sa hwole (Lilith for Lunars, Tepet Ejava for Dragon-Blooded, Prince of Shadows for Abyssals, and Chejob Kejak for Sidereals). They featured in more fiction and a lot of cover art and some of the stock images. 2e used mostly teh same ones, but also did kind of try to draw a lot of previously-named characters from the Caste and Aspect books and other soruces into art, ficiton, and references hwere ti could. I think actually 2e suffered a bit from over-use fo them. In 3e, the sigs are the characters you see in teh splats for Solars and DBs, who are new this editon and are a bit more back to being sample characters.<br /> <br /> Kind of pedantic, but thought would have been kind of cool to add.<br /> <br /> <b>Pronouns</b><br /> Something I did hear I wanted to note is that Exalted actually is kind of purposeful with the use of &quot;she&quot; for pronouns that other WW games aren't. Other WW games alternate between she and he, defaulting to she first. But Exalted actually does use it for mechanical purposes that you note. In Charms, the Charm's user/active character is always using the feminine pronouns. &quot;The Exalted uses her power to...&quot; or &quot;She rolls her...&quot; sort of thing. The target of a power's effects, by contrast, get the masculine ones. So Charms foten have &quot;She uses her Charm against his defense&quot; sort of format and does this pretty consistently in the Charms, Martial Arts, Sorcery, and Evocations and post-creobook books. The only spots it doesn't do it as consistently is sytems, but I think beyond that, it's always been she-as-default for generic mechanics.<br /> <br /> This is actually to me a perk. I have been finding that something of the flip-flopping in CofD books has kind of gotten on my nerves, as I find Exalted's being consisten there helps in readability when you know it's there.<br /> <br /> <b>The Caul</b><br /> Generally cool stuff and observations on the way the Caul works. I loved the Fire Shrine imagery best of your ideas of what they looked like. As for adventures, I think that while the goal is weird for PCs, you note pretty well I think it'd be a great game just for the adventure. Glory in itself or securing a great marraige prospect I think would also be cool motivations for it.<br /> <br /> Anywho, fun stuff. Looking forward for the next one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:44:29-07:00","id":1237004,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> \u201cCannon Characters\u201d was exactly the phrase that fits! Thanks for that!<br /> <br /> I appreciate your comments on the rest as well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T04:39:50-07:00","id":1237931,"title":"","content":"Episode 13 is live! In this one we take another deep dive into the Lunars playtest, this time breaking down our exploration into nine Lunar archetypes (three for each of the Attribute categories: physical, social, and mental). We also try to answer every question we could collect around the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:50:24-07:00","id":1240368,"title":"","content":"Episode 14 is live! In this one we get to sit down and talk with Exalted developer Eric Minton! We talk all about the setting, the books, the upcoming books, the not-yet-announced books, plus we ask him all the questions we could farm from around the interwebs.<br /> <br /> Character Seed of the Week: Oathbreaking Warrior (from listener Jeffrey!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T03:40:13-07:00","id":1240379,"title":"","content":"Great episode as always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T04:59:38-07:00","id":1240392,"title":"","content":"....<br /> Not done yet. But. <br /> <br /> RULES LIGHT EXALTED?!?<br /> DO WANT! RATHER NOW THAN LATER!<br /> <br /> Seriously, I have a big crowd of folks who have eyed Exalted and been scared away by the heftiness of the rules. Please, let's make this a reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T02:32:54-07:00","id":1243155,"title":"","content":"Episode 15 is live! In this one, we discuss whether or not you should teach new players about the ancient history of the Exalted universe, and how you might and might not want to use such history in your games. We also attempt to answer a listener\u2019s question about the differences in Exalt power levels.<br /> <br /> Story Seed of the Week: A Wild Accord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T06:21:42-07:00","id":1243190,"title":"","content":"Re: the Dragon-Blooded as gods thing, that is not the mainline Immaculate belief which holds that they're the most spiritually enlightened of humans and thus the ones most well suited to serving as intercessors with gods. The Cult background is in fact illegal and heretical in the Realm and Lookshy both<br /> <br /> In Prasad however their divergent variant of the faith has them placed firmly as elemental gods and receiving worship. I am all kinds of excited to be hearing more about Prasad in the Heirs to the Shogunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T07:35:42-07:00","id":1243206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1243155#post1243155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Episode 15 is live! In this one, we discuss whether or not you should teach new players about the ancient history of the Exalted universe, and how you might and might not want to use such history in your games. We also attempt to answer a listener\u2019s question about the differences in Exalt power levels.<br /> <br /> Story Seed of the Week: A Wild Accord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't had a chance to listen yet, but I try to keep things in new Chronicles to threes. Three factions nearby. Three notable NPCs (within or outside of those factions). Three parts of the local geography (be they regions or districts of town). And so on. <br /> <br /> That way there's no strict us-vs-them tribalism before the story can discover it. There's also no reason to drop the Encyclopaedia Exaeltica on them just yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T08:49:03-07:00","id":1243217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1243206#post1243206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haven't had a chance to listen yet, but I try to keep things in new Chronicles to threes. Three factions nearby. Three notable NPCs (within or outside of those factions). Three parts of the local geography (be they regions or districts of town). And so on.<br /> <br /> That way there's no strict us-vs-them tribalism before the story can discover it. There's also no reason to drop the Encyclopaedia Exaeltica on them just yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh, I like this idea A LOT! I am going to utilize this in my next session, since we basically had to start over. Stupid powerful Lunars... LOL!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T08:55:13-07:00","id":1243219,"title":"","content":"Yeah, generally gods are understood to be things that probably aren't doing their jobs if you can see them. <br /> <br /> Dragonblooded are what mortals should go fetch if they see any other magical things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T11:33:45-07:00","id":1243255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1243217#post1243217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooooh, I like this idea A LOT! I am going to utilize this in my next session, since we basically had to start over. Stupid powerful Lunars... LOL!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been trying to re-figure my own guidelines. After a long gaming career of building enormous messes that land like confusion-bombs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T11:38:35-07:00","id":1243256,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it, it would probably be worth writing up a short summary of \u201cThis is what your character knows about the setting\u201d for each character at the beginning of the game. It wouldn\u2019t need to be long, just a paragraph or set of bullet points about the local area. It\u2019s probably more useful to new players than trying to cram the entire cosmology down their throats all at once and, if they\u2019re experienced players, that can help them play more accurately so they don\u2019t have their dude from podunk nowhere rattle off the history of the Primordial War without thinking about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T11:43:14-07:00","id":1243258,"title":"","content":"I feel like the lore background needs to be taken into account somewhere too. <br /> <br /> Alternately, if a player knows the setting, get them to take a bit of lore so they have an excuse to know some of the stuff in-character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T21:13:38-07:00","id":1243391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1243258#post1243258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the lore background needs to be taken into account somewhere too. <br /> <br /> Alternately, if a player knows the setting, get them to take a bit of lore so they have an excuse to know some of the stuff in-character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. You should take into account the entirety of a character\u2019s background when you write something like what I was suggesting. Lore rating would factor in heavily, but so could lots of other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T21:28:04-07:00","id":1243393,"title":"","content":"Oh, yes. This is also an area where past life memories can be useful. If you want to give someone a brief glimpse of the deep past, to help with context and create a feel of epic scope to the game, give them a brief dream of something their past life experienced.<br /> <br /> You can also have the memories bleed over if a character wants to learn something that would fit their past life well and they don\u2019t really have any other means of knowing it. They should still spend the xp obviously, but it can be kinda fun (or creepy) to just wake up one morning and realize you know kung fu. Or suddenly remember a thousand years of training when you first grasp a sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T23:16:56-07:00","id":1244394,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4164_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4164\" data-vbnamecard=\"4164\">Lukkychukky</a> re: power levels, there are some brief guidelines in the Antagonists section when it comes to dicepools and competency, but one thing that will greatly help in judging a combat's difficulty will be some basic dice math. With a target number of 7 and double 10's, a dicepool has an average success rate of about 50%, with a slight swinginess upward. Depending on how into probabilities and statistics you are into we can pull in charts and stuff, but even without that you can know roughly how easily someone can hit or be hit based off that number. As pools get higher, most of the dice tricks add about another 5 or 10 percent on top of that.<br /> <br /> If you feel like playing with it, <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/1046\" target=\"_blank\">https://anydice.com/program/1046</a> plots the basic probability of 10d10 in Exalted. If you select &quot;At Least&quot; you'll see percentage chance of success for a given value.<br /> So you'd see that 75% of the time, 10d10 will get you 4 or more successes.<br /> <br /> So you can kinda SWAG some stuff based on that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12730_4.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12730\" data-vbnamecard=\"12730\">PneumaPilot</a> Not to be the loathsome forum canon police, but in all editions Creation has always firmly not been the body of Gaia. Her and Cytherea did some sort of primordial crazyness and created it, and she has some strong ties to it given that the Elemental Dragons are her children, but it isn't a similar situation to Malfeas or Autocthonia.<br /> <br /> Really digging the show guys, and I should have a question recorded for you soon! And it won't be forum nitpickyness, or moderately advanced math based!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 08-10-2018, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T05:19:00-07:00","id":1244451,"title":"","content":"Actually, while I'm not into statistics really, maybe I should delve a bit further into some of those charts. They're just kind of hard to understand, If I were to be honest. Thank you for the suggestions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T05:44:51-07:00","id":1244454,"title":"","content":"It might be an interesting 'cast to talk through Antagonist creation and see if you can find a minimal-math way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T07:23:28-07:00","id":1244478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1244454#post1244454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be an interesting 'cast to talk through Antagonist creation and see if you can find a minimal-math way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh. I really like this idea. Like, a lot. I'm going to pitch this for an upcoming episode. Not tomorrow's, and not next week's, since we have another very special guest. But the one after that, for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:01:01-07:00","id":1244537,"title":"","content":"My minimal math method would be to get a quick stateline from each of your players that has their attack, damage, defense, and Join Battle at minimum, but you might as well get their social influence stuff with their resolve, guile, appearance, per+Socialize, and whatever their best social pool is. <br /> <br /> Using the \u201c2 dice = 1 success\u201d rule of thumb, you can use those numbers to compare to the attacks and defenses of an antagonist and go \u201cOn average, they\u2019ll be able to hit this guy no problem\u201d or \u201cthey\u2019ll need to pump essence to hit this guy\u201d or \u201cok, they can hit this one no problem, but she has enough soak they\u2019ll only do their Overwhelming damage\u201d and so on. Same for their defenses.<br /> <br /> Granted it\u2019s more work than the challenge rating system, but you really can\u2019t just go \u201coh they\u2019re essence 3 now, I better get a group of essence 2 opponents together.\u201d Exalted is highly customizable. I\u2019m actually working on an Essence 5 Solar who can successfully take out an army but will get spanked in single combat with a skilled mortal. That\u2019s just not something you can do in Pathfinder, because of how the base attack bonus works.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll grant that there are lots of ways you can get various bonuses and methods for leveling the playing field in Pathfinder (I had a level 4 Ranger with a +17 stealth bonus) but that game is set up so that the playing field can only be leveled so much. A low level Rogue just really can\u2019t deal enough damage to one shot a high level Fighter and, once they\u2019re out of stealth, the Rogue is dead.<br /> <br /> Conversely, in Exalted, if you have a high Join Battle and Stealth pool and your opponent\u2019s Awareness sucks, you stand a decent chance of assassinating them with a single big Decisive on the first turn, regardless of who\u2019s Exalted and who\u2019s not, let alone your relative essence levels. There are enough ways of approaching Exalted and methods to force your opponent to fight you where you\u2019re strong and they\u2019re not that you can\u2019t just assume \u201cOh, I\u2019m an Essence 5 Solar therefore I win the game.\u201d That line of thought will get you killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 08-10-2018, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:47:18-07:00","id":1244557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1244451#post1244451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, while I'm not into statistics really, maybe I should delve a bit further into some of those charts. They're just kind of hard to understand, If I were to be honest. Thank you for the suggestions!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The antagonist charts, or the Anydice charts?<br /> <br /> I only took intro to stats in college, but I remember when I was first linked to anydice a couple years ago, it was pretty overwhelming, but then in a fit of mania I stayed up all night playing with it, and then at the end I was like Neo seeing matrix code.<br /> <br /> The thing that helped me the most with anydice (after I got the hang of the syntax) was changing the view to Graph, and the data to At Least, so that in most simple terms, you look at the x axis to find your target, and then find the point on the graph to tell you your chance of making it, or greater<br /> <br /> This also helped me appreciate fistful of d10 systems vs one big D systems, in that you gain the benefit of probability on your side. To put it succinctly, the more rolls you have the more it mitigates fluke rolls. Ye ole experiment of flipping a coin however many times and calculating the results of heads v tails, if you only flip like 3 times you could very easily have 100% heads, abut as you roll more you get closer to the expected 50%.<br /> <br /> Aaaanndd I just math nerded out, didn't I? Sorry.<br /> I might take it as a project to make a quick reference chart for Attack V Damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T02:55:38-07:00","id":1245375,"title":"","content":"Episode 16 is live! In this one, we talk all about Liminals: the facts we know, the possibilities, and ways we can use them in games both now and in the future! We also answer a listener question about designing epic cities.<br /> <br /> We also issued a challenge this week! Will you join us in creating one new Liminal Charm? Let your imaginations run wyld!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T10:50:38-07:00","id":1246386,"title":"","content":"Surprised <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12730_4.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12730\" data-vbnamecard=\"12730\">PneumaPilot</a> didn't mention that Liminals made their Debut in the penultimate 2nd edition book, Masters of Jade which featured a Liminal on the cover, with additional art and a namedrop on page 50 for Dame Crimson. She and her Guild associate Casim Thurat can also be seen in the Ex3 core on page 86.<br /> <br /> There's a passage referencing them on MoJ page 43, in regards to fighting a Lunar, in a classic comic book case of confused heroes fighting each other for the same cause-<br /> &quot;Eventually, the Guild, citing the power of the<br /> ghosts and their champion, enlisted the aid of one of the<br /> Liminal Exalted. As the two champions did battle under<br /> the darkness of a moonless sky, neither could gain the<br /> advantage. But the Liminal soon realized that it was the<br /> Guild that had brought death to the region, and it was<br /> only by the Guild\u2019s defeat that the ghosts would return<br /> to the lands of the dead. Showing no signs of flagging,<br /> the Chernozem withdrew from battle and returned to<br /> the Underworld to face the judgment of his dark mother.&quot;<br /> <br /> While looking through the Core for additional appearances, I finally realized one of the art pieces I wasn't really fond of on page 343 actually has Shen using Solar healing charms on Dame Crimson. I'm no longer convinced that is her own arm he is sowing on to her. This art piece has now endeared itself to me a little more.<br /> <br /> I also hadn't realized until now that their excellency cap jumps to Attribute+Essence when their anima is flaring.<br /> <br /> Another fun little quirk I think is of note, is that the process of creating a liminal distinctly parallels to the process of making an Alchemical exalted, what with the mortal labor of creation, and needing the divine intervention of a higher power (Dark Mother for Liminals, while AutoC doles out some Demiurge).<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I'm not trying to be the forum canon police, just wanted to further the conversation.<br /> <br /> Really enjoyed this episode, and I'm glad you guys got on the Liminal band wagon. While it may seem like all the new Exalt types can feel shoe-horned or extraneous, I really like that it opens up the setting even further. Things started to really feel paint by numbers in late 2e, where you would just spin the wheel or reference a random table to decide what the powerhouse in the area was, but breaking up the rigid pre-ordained cosmology has felt so freeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 08-15-2018, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T20:41:32-07:00","id":1247278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1246386#post1246386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While looking through the Core for additional appearances, I finally realized one of the art pieces I wasn't really fond of on page 343 actually has Shen using Solar healing charms on Dame Crimson. I'm no longer convinced that is her own arm he is sowing on to her. This art piece has now endeared itself to me a little more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! She is, isn't she. Nice spotting that easter egg.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T07:26:56-07:00","id":1247375,"title":"","content":"Hahaha! I\u2019ll have to shame him with this when we record today!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T18:38:03-07:00","id":1247577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1247375#post1247375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahaha! I\u2019ll have to shame him with this when we record today!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On the one hand I wasn't trying to be all &quot;well actually&quot;, but if it furthers the sniping banter then I'm all for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T09:06:26-07:00","id":1248085,"title":"","content":"Episode 17 is live! In this one, we get the privilege of interviewing Onyx Path\u2019s own Dixie Cochran! We talk to her about the game, the publishing aspects, the future schedule, and a whole bunch of other tangentially related stuff! We also wade through a pile of listener-submitted Liminal Charms!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T09:07:44-07:00","id":1248086,"title":"","content":"Episode 17 is live with special guest Dixie Cochran. Join us as we dive into the secret behind the scenes knowledge contained under that lovely green hair!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T02:37:59-07:00","id":1249085,"title":"","content":"Episode 18 is live! In this one, we talk about warstriders and how to potentially use them in a game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T06:38:51-07:00","id":1249111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1249085#post1249085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and how to potentially use them in a game!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've managed to accidentally use one as an unintended local cryptid in the region my game is set in which isn't their intended use of &quot;hammer of an angry god&quot; as they're statted but its been fun so far<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Also as I listen through the episode during lulls in work, I guess you guys and I were watching very different anime as kids or teens when it comes to thinking about <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LC0ryW5oM1w\" target=\"_blank\">Ascendant Nova Phoenix </a> and <a href=\"https://youtu.be/A89blUjT7z8\" target=\"_blank\">Karvara</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","user":"Alpharius","date":". 08-27-2018, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T11:07:53-07:00","id":1249177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1249111#post1249111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Also as I listen through the episode during lulls in work, I guess you guys and I were watching very different anime as kids or teens when it comes to thinking about <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/LC0ryW5oM1w&amp;quot;]Ascendant</a> Nova Phoenix [/URL] and <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/A89blUjT7z8&amp;quot;]Kaurava</a> [/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I\u2019ve never watched either of those. I did watch a fair bit of Robotech when I lived in Germany in the early 80s, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T11:21:14-07:00","id":1249179,"title":"","content":"That's totally fair. Ascendant Nova Phoenix being the Wing Gundam is a bit debatable but Karvara appears to have been designed from its official art to its Evocations to evoke Evangelion directly. Though the comparison you guys made with it to Nausicaa is pretty neat, especially since Eva and Nausicaa share a bit of DNA and the creator of the show worked on Nausicaa and was the animator of some of the more visually complex ending stuff...including the God Warrior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T13:13:05-07:00","id":1249200,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for real though you can actually match up some of Karvara's charms with specific scenes in Eva. <br /> <br /> And the core concept, an otherworldly being bound into the form of a mecha that can go berserk... that's an Evangelion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T19:02:35-07:00","id":1249246,"title":"","content":"Vance, who made Karvara, has explicitly stated that it's a reference to Neon Genesis Evangelion.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say I don't like Nausica\u00e4, because I do. It's just worth calling out an explicit reference, especially since you guys might find that series interesting. <br /> <br /> Also, as long as we're on Miyazaki, I'm gonna say that Castle in the Sky and Princess Mononoke are both good Exalted fodder.<br /> <br /> As for behemoths, there are three entities that fit that categorization in the Hundred Devils Night Parade series:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/212466/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Doppleganger-and-MataYadh-Demon?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/212466.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/212466/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Doppleganger-and-MataYadh-Demon?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\"> Hundred Devils Night Parade: Doppleganger and Mata-Yadh (Demon) - Onyx Path Publishing | Exalted 3rd Edition | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/212466/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Doppleganger-and-MataYadh-Demon?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/212466/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Doppleganger-and-MataYadh-Demon?cPath=8329_24225 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hundred Devils Night Parade: Doppleganger and Mata-Yadh (Demon) - From the frozen North to the burning South, and all directions in between, there are creatures that stalk Creation. Demo </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/238142/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Eight-Tailed-Mole-Hound-and-Mahicara-the-Volcanic-Earthwalker?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/238142.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/238142/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Eight-Tailed-Mole-Hound-and-Mahicara-the-Volcanic-Earthwalker?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\"> Hundred Devils Night Parade: Eight Tailed Mole Hound and Mahicara, the Volcanic Earthwalker - Onyx Path Publishing | Exalted 3rd Edition | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/238142/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Eight-Tailed-Mole-Hound-and-Mahicara-the-Volcanic-Earthwalker?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/238142/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Eight-Tailed-Mole-Hound-and-Mahicara-the-Volcanic-Earthwalker?cPath=8329_24225 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hundred Devils Night Parade: Eight Tailed Mole Hound and Mahicara, the Volcanic Earthwalker - From the frozen North to the burning South, and all directions in between, there are creatures that stalk Creation. Demo </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/215086/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Strix-and-Zicnal?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/215086.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/215086/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Strix-and-Zicnal?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\"> Hundred Devils Night Parade: Strix and Zicnal - Onyx Path Publishing | Exalted 3rd Edition | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/215086/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Strix-and-Zicnal?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/215086/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Strix-and-Zicnal?cPath=8329_24225 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hundred Devils Night Parade: Strix and Zicnal - From the frozen North to the burning South, and all directions in between, there are creatures that stalk Creation. Demo </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Granted, Zicnal is a person, not a monster, but he does have Legendary Size and a lot of power that is mystic in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T20:52:38-07:00","id":1249267,"title":"","content":"Oh, going back to your conversation with Dixie about Maps and stuff. I have no idea how hard it is to set up, but RedBubble apparently does sell Posters, Canvas Prints, and Tapestries, so I'd think there should be some options for selling Exalted Maps through them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T09:06:35-07:00","id":1249432,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that warstriders also help you fight like, elephants and titanic blood worms. Those things don't fuck around.<br /> <br /> <b>Hyperion</b> getting mentioned is pretty neat since that's one of my favorite books and the Shrike is actually my go-to example of an Ishvarra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T09:11:30-07:00","id":1249433,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s hard to overestimate how much I was in love with Hyperion while reading it. I haven\u2019t yet been able to make much progress through Endymion, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T14:25:32-07:00","id":1249531,"title":"","content":"One of the things I really love about All Conquering Colossus is its backstory. There\u2019s an implication in it that suggests that this might be the very first Warstrider ever, but it\u2019s also a love story. <br /> <br /> A love story about trying to win over a Monster Slaying Ultimate Bad-Ass by building a Giant Mech for her to wear and just Slaughter Everything in! (And also help keep her safe).<br /> <br /> So, you know, kinda Metal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T21:10:31-07:00","id":1249607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1249246#post1249246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance, who made Karvara, has explicitly stated that it's a reference to Neon Genesis Evangelion.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say I don't like Nausica\u00e4, because I do. It's just worth calling out an explicit reference, especially since you guys might find that series interesting. <br /> <br /> Also, as long as we're on Miyazaki, I'm gonna say that Castle in the Sky and Princess Mononoke are both good Exalted fodder.<br /> <br /> As for behemoths, there are three entities that fit that categorization in the Hundred Devils Night Parade series:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/212466/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Doppleganger-and-MataYadh-Demon?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ath=8329_24225</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/238142/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Eight-Tailed-Mole-Hound-and-Mahicara-the-Volcanic-Earthwalker?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ath=8329_24225</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/215086/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Strix-and-Zicnal?cPath=8329_24225\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ath=8329_24225</a><br /> <br /> Granted, Zicnal is a person, not a monster, but he does have Legendary Size and a lot of power that is mystic in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation was another overt mecha reference, specifically Heavy Arms' Endless Waltz variant.<br /> <br /> And on the behemoth thing, while none of them are explicitly behemoths, a bunch of the creatures in HDNP either already have legendary size or have the little &quot;and here's how you make it legendary size&quot; blurb","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 08-29-2018, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T22:13:37-07:00","id":1249614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1249433#post1249433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s hard to overestimate how much I was in love with Hyperion while reading it. I haven\u2019t yet been able to make much progress through Endymion, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of my feeling. <b>Hyperion</b> and <b>The Fall of Hyperion</b> are two of my favorite books ever. I have not had much energy or care to read anything in the latter half ot he Cantos in part because it ended so well I don't even really see the point of the Part Two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T10:24:45-07:00","id":1249726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1249614#post1249614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of my feeling. <b>Hyperion</b> and <b>The Fall of Hyperion</b> are two of my favorite books ever. I have not had much energy or care to read anything in the latter half ot he Cantos in part because it ended so well I don't even really see the point of the Part Two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I finished the Endymion books back then but i cheated ... skipped chapters whole, the romance parts and sacrificial lamb archetype were really not my thing. Was fun to see the Shrike getting the Terminator 2 treatment though ...<br /> <br /> About the Hyperion books ... don't we have a nice Solar Circle brewing here, in the Pilgrims?<br /> <br /> I mean, if any character ever deserved a Dawn Exaltation ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24379-hoardandsue","name":"HoardAndSue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T15:39:15-07:00","id":1251509,"title":"","content":"I tend to think of the Sisterhood of Pearls as being akin to one of the various Christian splinter faiths, with one half content to stay remote missionaries and the other half wanting to go back and nail a copy of the Five Criticisms on the door of the Palace Sublime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T02:43:04-07:00","id":1252994,"title":"","content":"Episode 20 is live! In this one, we talk about whether or not published adventures should be a priority for Exalted, and we go ahead and design a Pathfinder-style epic Adventure Path for the game using the method we described back in episode 5! And we want to hear from you! Would you want published adventures like this? What do you think of the one we made?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T16:37:38-07:00","id":1253156,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I agree with you in concept, that Exalted could use some nice adventures and things (I\u2019m hoping the War in the West section will help out with that) but I do think that Exalted might have a couple of issues that make long Adventure Paths more difficult than they do in Pathfinder.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the Exalted in general and Solars in specific, have enough power and agency that it\u2019s not hard for them to derail things if they want to. So, if I were constructing an Adventure Path, I\u2019d try to make sure that the Players are really buying into the end goal of the thing and that the characters\u2019 goals also matched up well. I\u2019d also look for potential \u201cfailure points\u201d in the adventure, places where I assume things will go in a particular direction and either make notes about what to do if it doesn\u2019t happen that way or try to remove that particular choice from the Adventure.<br /> <br /> As for your specific example, it sounds pretty cool, but I think, now that you have all the bits worked out, you need to go back and try to make them fit together better so that it feels like one continuous story instead of a bunch of random vignettes connected together. Maybe take some of the early stuff and use it again later and pull some of the later stuff and insert foreshadowing for it early on.<br /> <br /> Also I think you need to cut Season 5. And the Airship.<br /> <br /> At the end of Season 4, you\u2019re rushing off to go get into the final battle. And then Season 5 sends you off to wander in the Wyld for who knows how long, instead of going off to save the Sun from getting ganked. I could see it working for a session, maybe, to help build tension, but after that the players are just gonna be frustrated at how long this is taking instead of having a fun romp through the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Also, Season 5 starts with one of those \u201cFailure Points\u201d I mentioned before. Specifically, it assumes that a bunch of Solar Exalted are going to lose a battle. Which... Ok, I\u2019m not gonna say I\u2019ve never seen Solars run from combat before or lose a fight or anything, but... I would never bet on team of Solars to lose a fight, no matter how bad the odds. And, if the Solars don\u2019t lose that fight, they\u2019re gonna bypass the entire Season. <br /> <br /> Based on my experience with Exalted, it would actually be very, very difficult to force the Solars to lose a fight without risking a TPK in the process, especially if I was trying to murder an NPC at the same time.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, assuming their ship did crash, if you have a Sorcerer or a Craft focused Solar on the team, they could either take a couple days and summon some First Circle riding demons or just fix the First Age ship and be on their way, again short circuiting the adventure.<br /> <br /> So...I think you either need to cut it or move it earlier in the path when time isn\u2019t such a big deal. And guard against those failure points I mentioned.<br /> <br /> As for the Airship, while it is cool...I feel like you should have the players capture it, recover it, dig it up, or something, instead of the Lunar saying \u201coh, yeah, I have the keys to the Five Metal Shrike in my pocket. Would that help?\u201d Alternately, if the Lunar has that Legendary Size charm and can turn into a giant Firebird that everyone can ride, I think that\u2019s probably just as awesome as a First Age Airship.<br /> <br /> Also, that undead Dragon King. You said one of the neverborn pulled a chunk of itself off and turned it into armor for the guy to wear? I think you can go bigger there. <br /> <br /> Two words<br /> <br /> Neverborn Warstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 09-10-2018, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:20:46-07:00","id":1253168,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of adventure paths. I've run several premade campaigns in other games, and in others have looted their premade stuff for some ideas even if I don't use it directly. However, Exalted has a major problem I feel in that the awesome powers available to a PC no matter what kind of Exalt they are makes it very hard to make any assumptions about how things will go.<br /> <br /> I'm going to compare this to another premade campaign I'm running right now, The Darkening of Mirkwood for The One Ring. The Darkening of Mirkwood takes place of 30 years of time in play with one provided adventure per year and suggestions for more if you want. After about six or seven years, things start showing up to the effect of 'if X NPC is dead/dishonored/you made them a foe, try to sub in a character who meets XYZ requirements'. By the end of the campaign there's precious few assumptions left and the adventures presented are mostly focused on the situations being created from the far side of the hero/villain line and the few guaranteed things left in the setting to help frame what you guys do. That isn't to say there's a lack of setting material or neat ideas, but basically the longer time goes on the less specific and more broad the strokes get. Though this going off the rails actually works out pretty well for the game, and the conclusion of it feels as epic as anything else LotR has ever offered and features ties between the Hobbit, the Silmarillion, and LotR.<br /> <br /> I mostly feel like an Exalted premade campaign will run into that problem of needing broad strokes even more strongly and basically immediately. Dragon-Blooded can do miracles that every possible GM can't prep for, let alone a Solar. Or forthcoming Lunars, Exigents, Sidereals, and more. It basically will become an exercise in planning for ways to encourage the party to stick to at least moderate rails which might be maddening for a writer, or an unfun railroad. I know this is a much maligned 2e product, but look at Return of the Scarlet Empress. There's so many contingencies and possible splits of story in there because a given circle of Exalted might lead to such different ends and arcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T19:21:26-07:00","id":1253192,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a> I would like to respond to a couple of your points. First, practically all of the &quot;Seasons&quot; in our example AP were viewed from extreme distance. Each one would need to be developed into a very lengthy 100-page adventure book for it to have the kind of length and epicosity to truly qualify for an Exalted AP. As such, Season 5 would have way more to it than just simply a Wyld romp. That is merely is the central activity of that Season. In a similar vein, note how the broad overview of Season 1 mentions nothing about a fishing competition, and yet in the more detailed view, these kinds of neat events start showing up. I have no doubt that if we really dug into Season 5, we could have some very strong connections to Season 4 and Season 6 that would make that little side-jaunt seem very much in the right place. I felt much the same as you when Jim wrote that Season as the precursor to my War in Heaven ending, but I believe that with some work, it could end up being one of the best parts of the whole AP.<br /> <br /> Second, I see everywhere (and hear it from some of the devs) that Exalted is just not the kind of game that could work well with a lengthy story (or just pre-written adventures in general) because the characters are too powerful, and the players will just not put up with being railroaded through some story, but I think that attitude is a bit dishonest. I could just as easily point out that D&amp;D or Pathfinder or Starfinder characters are agents with free will that would never put up with being railroaded through the long stories written for them (the very popular and lucrative long stories, I might add), and it would be true. Our Iron Gods group could easily have walked away from the whole mystery and threat right at the beginning in the town of Torch and derailed the whole adventure...but then we wouldn't be playing Iron Gods - a story that we all decided would be really awesome and fun to play through. But that is exactly why the Pathfinder AP's all have the Campaign Traits that really tie characters into the setting and goings on anyway. You are essentially choosing a player option that links you into the story.<br /> <br /> That being said, players will always derail a story a little bit, even when they WANT to do what they think they are 'supposed' to do to progress the story. I don't know if you've read a Pathfinder AP in a while, though. They're actually written very well, and I've almost never had trouble keeping players engaged in the fun. I pretty much defy the whole idea that such a thing can't be done for Exalted. Of course it can. But I would also say that even when you are preparing general situations for the players to face and leaving a lot of room open for player agency, players can still wreck the entire story, especially if they are misbehaving (maybe they're ticked at something, have indigestion, or whatever). This is actually the reason why Episode 2 of Wyld Shape is taking so long to be finished. We had to scrap the whole thing because of this very issue. But that could have easily happened in any Pathfinder AP with a player that just got it into his/her head to nuke the story.<br /> <br /> Third, I think it would be very easy to engineer a fight that Solars will lose. The airship itself is not a Solar exalt. A sufficient number of enemies targeting vital systems could absolutely bring the craft down. There are actual rules for this game. I've not seen any Charms that say, &quot;Pay 5m: win!&quot; In fact, all-in-all I'd say the 3E Charms are much weaker on average than 2E. And I think it would be very easy to prevent your Solar crafter from just rolling to save the day - you'd be deep behind enemy lines for one thing.<br /> <br /> I strongly believe that all role-playing games are a contract between gamemaster and players to tell a compelling story. Whether that story is massive and pre-written or completely homebrew with no prep beyond &quot;What did Onyx Path release this week in the HDNP and AotR?&quot; (looking at you, Chuck!) if the characters want to derail the story, they can. If they want to play the epic story you've devised, they can do that too. But in my mind, the absolute worst decision is just throwing up one's hands and saying, &quot;Well, THIS can't be done, so let's not even try!&quot;<br /> <br /> I appreciate your comments, and the chance to try to 'defend' against them a little bit - even though I know that you are not 'attacking' with your words. The whole point of this particular episode was to challenge some of these very notions. In my anecdotal experience, the people I've encountered online have by and large played a couple of games of Exalted, but never really stuck with it for very long. Almost every single soul that I've ever met or interacted with who played Pathfinder, on the other hand, have told me all about all of the different APs they've played through, and which ones they've played all the way to completion. The difference is staggering, and if Exalted ever has a chance to really experience some success, I firmly believe it's going to need some really good stories for people to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T05:19:05-07:00","id":1253255,"title":"","content":"Thanks for an interesting episode!<br /> <br /> While I agree with many of @BrilliantRain's points, I'm mostly satisfied with your counterarguments. I agree with your argument that roleplay is an agreement between the GM and the Players about playing a story together - still, I think there's a huge difference between players refusing to follow the story and requiring them to ignore skills their characters have to advance it in a predetermined way. I mainly refer to the choice between fixing the airship and having a Sorcerer conjure a demon, Stormwind raider or (if they're already Celestial Tier) Travelling without Distance. The hypothetical Sorcerer player has invested a lot of resources so they'd be allowed to do cool stuff with spells. So it is unfair and bad design to skip a significant part of the adventure, if the PC wants to use a basic tool in their kit. (It's comparable to forcing a stealth encounter by saying the Fighter is suddenly not allowed to knife a guard.)<br /> So I think your outline should at least provide a reason for the players to go to the Wyld even if they don't need the airship. (There are other smaller examples which I won't go into, unless you want.)<br /> <br /> On another point, I have a vehement dislike for battles that the players are supposed to lose, so I frown that you already have two (airship battle and the first one with the slavers). If the players cannot influence the outcome, why have a battle? Why not begin the adventure with the PC's already captured or the ship already crashed? If there is to be a battle, its outcome should matter - even (or some would say, especially) if it's unlikely. Do the PC's have to get caught in the beginning? If they fight well, could they Exalt in combat?<br /> <br /> The critique out of the way, I do think that your outline has a lot of interesting points: especially the ending, which I'm tempted to borrow parts for my own coming game. And I agree it shows that one can make adventure modules for Exalted.<br /> <br /> I'm actually interested in what else you have to offer and how you would flesh out your outline further!<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, I'd also like to see more open-ended adventures developed for Exalted. I think that the GUMSHOE method of adventure design could work even better for Exalted than the more rigid Pathfinder style. I think their flexible Scene-to-Scene style would suit a Circle, where the party might be hyperproficient in some areas, but lack even an Excellency in others. A critical difference between Exalted and Pathfinder is that Pathfinder characters can be assumed to be able to fight - and get better at it - at an even, measurable pace, while a Solar Exalted might not be able to fight at all and never get better at it. That's why a good Exalted adventure should have many solutions to any one problem. I could imagine a campaign style used in The Zalozhniy Quartet or Dracula Dossier easily adapted to the Exalted setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T05:51:39-07:00","id":1253259,"title":"","content":"I'll say that a lot of the challenges that have been noted don't make things impossible to make a fun Exalted adventure path but are complications to take into account mostly. Planning for wide scope of power and potential short circuits is doable and has been done before. A key part of a good adventure path is giving tools for less confident GMs to learn in whatever areas they feel less adept, since everyone has some strong and weak points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T08:08:40-07:00","id":1253288,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12596_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12596\" data-vbnamecard=\"12596\">Alpharius</a> Quite well said! I agree completely!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T13:01:56-07:00","id":1253362,"title":"","content":"It's notable that Exalted 1e did have an attempt of adventures in two places: <b>Time of Tumult </b>and <b>Exalted: the Aucothhonians</b>.<br /> <br /> Time of Tumult had three main scenarios. One was a two-parter, whcih is generally neat for some settinb uilding but is mostly forgettable since it's basically an Exalted reskin of a dungeon crawl deathtrap. I think getting to the Hidden Fortress is more itneresting, but is so early in the line it also doesn't quite line up very well with how the game eventaully evolved.<br /> <br /> I hear mixed on the &quot;Western Exiles&quot; story. But I think it's notable that it veers quite a bit from the Adventure Path thing liek Pathfidner does. It's more an outline,w here you kind of go through various vinettes, and encounter a diversity of beings. And it's also notably not like, that long. It takes a hwole chapter of a book, but I think not a lot like, happens that takes a lot. It is very much a start of a campaign, but I think is notably forgettable.<br /> <br /> The best scneario in that book was (to me at least) &quot;Crusaders of the Machine God&quot;. And it's notable to me how differently structured it is compared to a Pathfinder Adventue Path. It's very ST-facing, describing beforehand notable regions and things, and providing a timeline of events with &quot;How things go unelss PCs intervene and plot elements to work wtih from there.&quot; I think it pulled things off well for balance of regionalism (It was constrained mostly to the South and the consequences there) and how it presented the Yugashite forces as overwelming the region but having setbacks and becoming a new empire int ehre gion. It feels like you can use it in a lot of differetn ways and for a lot of didfferent games (I used parts of it half a dozen times over the years).<br /> <br /> The scenarios in <b>Exalted: the Autochthonians</b> by contrast...don't. THey provide a couple different takes. &quot;The Locust War&quot; tries It hink to retell CotMG, but it fails in that I think it misses scale, tries to do too much int he setting all at once, and isn't so good at integrating Alchemicals and Yugash into Creation without it seeming like a rollover. It was too apocalyptic in its toen and prone to just silly hyperbole. While the Crsuaders outline was good for being a neat &quot;Event in Creation&quot; in a bigger world, the Locust War is presented as something that like, defines the world and tirs to cover so much to get silly. It's the land memes were born from.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Great Source&quot; was I think the best of these scenarios. It presents an interesting setup, and plotline for PCs to get into. It uses a neat setting element (the Eye of Autochthon) and I think doesn't go too far in existential threat realm of things. It's just kind of odd since that after the Eye is found it becomes this paint-by-numbers world-adventure and I think needed more expansion on that. And it almsot to me loses out on what makes Autochthonia nintersting since it's so Creation-facing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Engines of Annihilation&quot; is an...interesting story, which also does the timeline thing. It just happens to also like &quot;The Locust War&quot; go into &quot;Total apocalypse mode&quot; with things so badly that it almost loses the thread of what makes Creation and Autochthonia interesting settings in the rpcoess. It's I think too much about Deathlord as existential threat and the consequences of dead Primordials than it is about like, stories for charcters ina way. It is a neat idea I think in the end wasnt' needed.<br /> <br /> The only other 1e storyline like these I think was Swar in <b>Bastions of the North</b>, but I don't generally here much folks tlak about it and I barelyr emember it myself. It's basically again an exotic environment characters just kind of poke at with vinettes and nto a lot happesnt here beyond what the ST does with I think.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think it stands out that the most useful adventure for Exalted sin't an Adventure Path, but a event outline. Exalted just as a whole operates often on scales and with enough break-points as defined above that trying to boil it down to specific interactions and such loses a lot of what makes Exalted, even in a more combat-orientated style, hard to encapsulate into such a setup. <br /> <br /> Now note, <b>Heirs to the Shogunate</b> apparently is going ot have two new scenarios, which use &quot;The Locust Crusade&quot; as their style templates: &quot;Realm Civil War&quot; and &quot;The War in the West&quot;. I kind of hope future companion books bring about similar scenario thingies, as I think thsoe are really cool and for most games, going to be more usefult han another &quot;Hidden Fortress&quot; or whateve the hell happened in <b>Return of the Scarlet Empress</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T13:09:16-07:00","id":1253364,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> Thanks for the insightful coverage of all of those scenarios!<br /> <br /> I think it would be foolish to ever give up on trying to make an awesome AP for Exalted just because it has never been done before, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T13:15:17-07:00","id":1253365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1253364#post1253364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> Thanks for the insightful coverage of all of those scenarios!<br /> <br /> I think it would be foolish to ever give up on trying to make an awesome AP for Exalted just because it has never been done before, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's also something to be said on resources and time there.<br /> <br /> White Wolf did do some adventures (The Giovanni Chornicles, the Ventrue Chronices, the By Night books, and so on) but by the tiem fo Exalted, started moving away from them in general I find. The developers also in general I think have always preferred more setting content useful to more games in general versus adventure paths which while useful for some games, aren't as useufl for the world as a whoel. Note that Creation in general is much, <i>much</i> larger than the default region in a standard D&amp;D fantasy setting, so there is also more room that just needs covered by the game as a whole.<br /> <br /> During 2e this was just kind of continued and it seemed like while attempts were done with the SAS, it just never took off in the end. (I liked and started a game with <b>Daughter of Nexus </b>myself, though). There were two such adventures in 2e at least: <b>Daughter of Nexus</b> and <b>Contagion of Law</b>. They're neat, but It hink a big thing is it's notable production levels foa typical 2e Exalted book to a Paizo or WotC book. The amount of budget Exalted gets in general with manpower, art assets, and writing means that choices were made and I think in geenral, the devs have always opted for what they found more useful for more games. Which often is books that have lots of plot hooks, rather than fewer more detailed plots. A Gazetter like <b>Blood &amp; Salt</b> which also has story seeds in it is going to be more suefl than a module for moe players I think. This is arguably a flaw with 2e, which often didn't do this quite so well or often took plot hooks and just spilled them out as something happening already instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T14:08:47-07:00","id":1253375,"title":"","content":"Right. I understand their thinking about what would be a better use of time, manpower, money, etc., I just also think it\u2019s a misstep. That was my point in the episode, to say that a game like Pathfinder, with its model, has managed to produce a living world full of deep setting information, while simultaneously producing a LOT of adventure content that actually sells the game (and shows people how to play). <br /> <br /> And I think that the writers/decision makers look at the outcome of something like the SAS and think, \u201cWell, that wasn\u2019t as successful as we would have liked, so adventures must not be the best use of our time and resources,\u201d but that\u2019s not comparing apples to apples. Hold up the Rise of the Runelords Anniversary Edition against those two SAS modules and ask yourself if they even belong in the same plane of existence. Of course they don\u2019t! But what if Exalted DID have its own RotR, in its own flavor? I think the game would be much more of a hit than it currently is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T23:28:53-07:00","id":1253502,"title":"","content":"For the record, I do think Adventures for Exalted can be done. I do like the Adventure Path concept and I\u2019ve even been trying to brainstorm my own, for use with the Storyteller\u2019s Vault later on. <br /> <br /> But I think it\u2019s important to look at places where, as the author, you\u2019re assuming things will go one way and consider what happens if things don\u2019t go that way. Yes, granted, sometimes the answer to that is \u201cwell, if they don\u2019t grab the adventure hook, I guess we\u2019ll see what\u2019s on the X-Box instead\u201d but sometimes there are entirely reasonable responses to a situation that need to be considered instead of just ignored.<br /> <br /> But then, I guess that\u2019s what playtesting is for.<br /> <br /> I mean, your proposed Adventure Path introduces flying enemies fairly early on. I like playing thinky types and Sorcerers, so, if I were playing it, assuming I didn\u2019t go for Cirrus Skiff during Exalted character creation (it\u2019s a cool spell with a very nice control bonus and it\u2019s scary with a ranged combat build), it\u2019s probably gonna be on my \u201cto buy\u201d list once the flying Dragon Kings show up. Because flying enemies can be really hard to deal with if you can\u2019t fly yourself, so learning to fly is a logical response. And, even if I didn\u2019t get Cirrus Skiff, I probably did get Demon of the First Circle so summoning one that can fly me around would be a logical and reasonable action from my point of view at that point.<br /> <br /> And then, much later on, if I can ferry around a Dawn to fight people outside the ship, it will likely change the dynamic of that entire fight. I mean, the Essence 4 Dawn in my game launched an attack that would have entirely destroyed a Size 4 Battlegroup of First Circle demons (it ended up doing 58 lethal HLs of damage, which was exactly enough to reduce a Battlegroup of those demons from Size 4 to Size 0. Pity the Battlegroup was only Size 1). It was under near perfect circumstances and it used up most of his mote pool, but it\u2019s a thing he can do. I kinda suspect that the Solars would have similar power by that point in the Adventure Path, so if you want to crash the ship, they\u2019ll need a very good reason not to just go outside and kill everyone. Falling from the sky would seem to be a deterrent, but, as noted, Cirrus Skiff, summoned Agata, flight artifacts, the acrobatic Dawn saying \u201cHey, watch this!\u201d and then leaping from Dragon King to Dragon King while murdering them, and so on.<br /> <br /> Which probably means that Flight powers should be addressed early on in the AP. Either make it part of the social contract with a note at the beginning saying \u201caccess to flight and fast travel is going to be a big deal in this adventure, so make sure that the players are aware that they probably shouldn\u2019t pick up those kinds of powers\u201d or something, or redesign the adventure a bit so that it\u2019s not a huge deal if the players can fly around on their own.<br /> <br /> Really, that\u2019s all I\u2019m saying. Once you get into the details and playtesting, things will likely happen that may necessitate a rewrite of a good chunk of the AP or at least some helpful notes. But I don\u2019t think it\u2019s impossible to do a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T23:38:33-07:00","id":1253504,"title":"","content":"Right now, I think the main issue standing in the way of Exalted getting Adventure Paths is the fact that they apparently have enough writers to handle like one or two books at a time. So doing an Adventure Path basically means they\u2019d have to push whatever the next splat was off for a year, which I don\u2019t think they\u2019re ready to do.<br /> <br /> I suspect that the best way to get a good Adventure Path for Exalted will be to write and publish one once Exalted gets added to the Storyteller\u2019s Vault and see what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T04:49:43-07:00","id":1254972,"title":"","content":"Episode 21 is live! In this one, we talk about the results from our Adventure Path polls and take a bit more of a dive into Dragon Kings!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T21:17:37-07:00","id":1255170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1213529-the-deliberative-a-new-weekly-exalted-podcast?p=1254972#post1254972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Episode 21 is live! In this one, we talk about the results from our Adventure Path polls and take a bit more of a dive into Dragon Kings!</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple things that stood out in the podcast:<br /> <br /> - Dragon-Kings were actually in 1e too. They first got talked about in <b>Ruins of Rathess</b> and there were full rules for them in the <b>Exalted Player's Guide</b> save for the Dark Paths, actually.<br /> <br /> - Tortured Bodhisatva is the best path and Murder Samsara and Wear Her Sad Robes is the best Step name, damn it.<br /> <br /> - Liminals actually pretty purposefully <i>don't</i> follow the corpse elements from Abyssals. Their Aspects are Blood, Breath, Flesh, Marrow, and Soil, more well, &quot;threshold&quot; things between life and death, than simply death itself.<br /> <br /> - Remember human origins and such depends on edition. While the creators did make humans in 1e and 2e, we don't know why and what they gave a shit to them after that isn't clear, so the humans then siding iwth the gods is moot if they went on spending millennia just being humans in the world after that.<br /> <br /> - There are actually some Dragon King sin Heaven, which gets missed abit.<br /> <br /> - Pterok is pronounced &quot;terok&quot; I think. The P is silent like in Pteranodon.<br /> <br /> - Mosok, Anklok, and Raptok are also based on extinct repitles, namely mososaurs, anklylosaurs, and raptors I Think.<br /> <br /> - I would argue on reincarnation, Dragon Kings are actually more like the Avatar than Exalted are. A thing of note is that while you are encouraged to pick up a bit where you left off, each life for the Dragon King is still a new person. They can even be born into different Breeds I think between lives. To me it is a bit more like tapping into the Avatar Cycle than what Exalts do. To me, Exalts the best way to describe them i s less a soul and more like...a title. You inherit the Exaltation and it's almost this legacy that's foisted onto you and the privileges and obligations attached to it. Your memories are sparse and such from there but you don't so much talk to yoru past but tap into some elements useful for your current power.<br /> <br /> - Remember that Djala and beastfolk are sitll human in Creation. Creation just has a pretty wide breadth as to what counts as human.<br /> <br /> - I think the devs said they plan to have them as potential character things in the future, but like most things, they gotta wait for other stuff like Exalts first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T02:37:26-07:00","id":1256908,"title":"","content":"Episode 22 is live! In this one, we talk about making two-dot artifacts, and we make a few of our own! Plus, all the resource and art packs are now available for Storyteller\u2019s Vault.","signature